NV_PK(6,{"the caul fat melts in the hot oil leaving a golden crispy skin while the shrimp inside stays sweet and springy some shops now wrap them in tofu skin instead":"","eat them with a little wasabi sauce or sweet chili sauce plus a bowl of shrimp soup or fish ball soup and you have the classic anping old street meal":"","anping is by the sea so seafood snacks like shrimp rolls and oyster omelets grew up there":"","the skin is crispy and the shrimp is sweet":"","is this fried to order":"","shrimp":"","a small sea animal with a long body and a shell":"","the shrimp rolls are fried to order":"","caul fat":"","a thin net like layer of fat from a pig used to wrap food":"","shrimp rolls are wrapped in caul fat":"","golden":"","having a warm yellow colour like gold":"","fry them until they turn golden":"","springy":"","wasabi":"","a very hot green paste from japan":"","shrimp rolls come with wasabi sauce":"","tainan people love rice for wa gui long grain rice is soaked and ground into a batter poured into small bowls topped with minced pork salted egg yolk mushroom and shrimp and steamed southern wa gui is light brown because braising liquid is mixed into the batter":"","you eat it not with chopsticks but with a flat bamboo spatula cutting it into small pieces and topping it with thick soy sauce and garlic it is smooth soft and full of rice flavour":""});